sales_costs = section('costs', '<div class="comparison-reading comparison-table-intro"><h2>Know what 20 bookings would cost.</h2><p>With our plans, 20 qualified booked meetings means $2,000 in meeting fees. Add the base fee for your chosen plan. These are monthly billing examples in USD, not a prediction of results.</p></div><p class="table-scroll-cue">Swipe to see the total for each plan.</p><div class="plan-table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Our monthly costs at 20 qualified booked meetings" tabindex="0"><table class="plan-comparison"><caption>The Revenue Inbox: monthly costs at 20 qualified booked meetings.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Plan</th><th scope="col">Base fee</th><th scope="col">20 meeting fees</th><th scope="col">Total</th></tr></thead><tbody>' + plan_rows + '</tbody></table></div><div class="comparison-reading comparison-after-table"><p><strong>Basic:</strong> $2,000 plus your actual vendor bills. You buy domains, mailboxes and tools directly and share access. <strong>Standard:</strong> $3,500 with managed infrastructure. <strong>Express:</strong> $4,500 with managed, prewarmed infrastructure for a day-3 launch.</p><p>SalesHive quotes an inclusive managed-program fee. Its pricing page does not publish dollar rates. Ask for your actual quote before calculating a cost difference; do not add its included team, data and software a second time. ' + source('pricing') + '.</p><p>For your decision, check the cost per accepted meeting, attendance and sales opportunities together. A booking fee and an SDR retainer pay for different things.</p><p><a href="/pricing">Explore our plans and pricing calculator ' + icon() + '</a></p></div>', 'tonal-section')

sales_fit = section('fit', '<div class="comparison-reading"><h2>Why choose The Revenue Inbox?</h2><h3>Start with a clear price for a qualified result.</h3><p>Our $100 fee is attached to a booked call with a decision-maker inside your agreed ICP who has agreed to hear the offer. A positive reply alone does not qualify. Agreeing the acceptance criteria before launch gives your team a concrete outcome to evaluate.</p><h3>Choose how much infrastructure you want us to own.</h3><p>Basic keeps the monthly agency base fee at $0. You pay vendors directly and give us access to run the campaign. Standard is $1,500 per month plus meeting fees; Express is $2,500 per month plus meeting fees. On both managed plans, we buy and manage the sending setup.</p><h3>Get a defined meeting commitment.</h3><p>Standard and Express include 20 qualified meetings in 30 days from campaign launch, or we work for free. Basic does not include this guarantee. Confirm the remedy, qualification rules and treatment of no-shows in your agreement.</p><h3>Move quickly when your campaign is ready.</h3><p>Express campaigns go live on day 3: three calendar days after payment, required inputs and approvals are complete. We use prewarmed domains and mailboxes. This is a launch commitment, separate from the 30-day meeting guarantee.</p><p>SalesHive describes a typical launch of about three weeks, subject to readiness. Those are different starting conditions, so compare the complete timeline for your campaign. ' + source('email') + '.</p><h3>Keep your team focused on closing.</h3><p>We own the email-led campaign, from ICP and list research to messaging, email and LinkedIn outreach, replies and booking. You take the sales calls. If that is the job you need handled, our plans give you a direct way to buy it.</p><p>A dedicated phone-led SDR team is a different brief. SalesHive provides that scope. Its email service also includes managed infrastructure and reply support. Choose our plans when your priority is a focused email-led campaign, published fees and an agreed qualified-booking outcome. ' + source('email') + '.</p></div>')

