cience_fit = section('fit', '<div class="comparison-reading"><h2>Why choose The Revenue Inbox?</h2><h3>Use one qualified-meeting fee across every plan.</h3><p>Basic, Standard and Express each charge $100 per qualified booked meeting. The base fee changes with infrastructure responsibility and launch speed. That gives you a straightforward model for checking the bill as booking volume changes.</p><p>We agree the ICP and qualification rules before launch. A billable meeting is a booked call with a decision-maker inside that ICP who has agreed to hear the offer. A positive reply alone does not qualify.</p><h3>Choose how you handle the infrastructure.</h3><p>On Basic, your monthly agency base fee is $0. You buy domains, mailboxes and tools directly and share access. On Standard at $1,500 per month or Express at $2,500 per month, we buy and manage the setup. Meeting fees apply on every plan.</p><h3>Put a commitment behind the bookings.</h3><p>Standard and Express include 20 qualified meetings in 30 days from campaign launch, or we work for free. Basic does not include this guarantee. Confirm qualification, acceptance criteria and the remedy in your agreement.</p><h3>Choose a defined launch timeline.</h3><p>Express campaigns go live on day 3: three calendar days after payment, required inputs and approvals are complete. We use prewarmed domains and mailboxes. This is a launch promise, separate from the 30-day meeting guarantee.</p><h3>Buy the scope your team needs.</h3><p>Our service suits teams that want email and LinkedIn outreach handled through to qualified booking while they run the sales calls. We own research, copy, infrastructure, replies and the booking handoff.</p><p>CIENCE also handles the work behind a booking, including human reply management. If your brief calls for a coordinated phone-led SDR team, include that scope when evaluating the options. ' + source('email') + '.</p><p>Track qualification, booked meetings, attendance and opportunities separately with either service. Published booking fees make the invoice easier to understand; your sales outcomes still depend on the offer, market and follow-through.</p></div>')

